{
    "background_story": "Marcel was a charming French artist who lived in the 1920s. He had a quirky habit of collecting matchbooks from every caf\u00e9 and restaurant he visited. Each matchbook told a story of a place he'd been, a person he'd met, or a memory he'd made. Marcel's friends would often tease him about his collection, but he saw beauty in the small, intricately designed covers. One day, while rummaging through his matchbook collection, Marcel stumbled upon a book from a quaint little bistro where he had met his future wife, Colette. The matchbook sparked a flood of memories, and Marcel was inspired to create a series of paintings depicting the caf\u00e9's vibrant atmosphere. His art gained popularity, and soon Marcel's matchbook collection became a symbol of his creative spark and the power of nostalgia.",
